1
00:00:01,375 --> 00:00:04,626
<i>Run, until we reach</i>

2
00:00:04,792 --> 00:00:09,209
<i>Until we reach you</i>

3
00:00:13,584 --> 00:00:17,250
<i>The clear blue open sea</i>

4
00:00:17,667 --> 00:00:20,250
<i>A sliver of a miracle</i>

5
00:00:21,167 --> 00:00:27,208
<i>We've encountered more
Than we could ever imagine</i>

6
00:00:27,209 --> 00:00:29,792
<i>With every step we take
On this journey</i>

7
00:00:29,959 --> 00:00:33,459
<i>The goal is still out of sight</i>

8
00:00:33,834 --> 00:00:37,292
<i>But we can overcome anything</i>

9
00:00:37,417 --> 00:00:40,501
<i>Just to see your smile</i>

10
00:00:40,626 --> 00:00:44,792
<i>If we wavered,
We couldn't shine</i>

11
00:00:44,959 --> 00:00:48,666
<i>We even strove to conquer
Our weaknesses</i>

12
00:00:48,667 --> 00:00:51,167
<i>We, who were truly devoted</i>

13
00:00:51,292 --> 00:00:54,208
<i>Have always been the same</i>

14
00:00:54,209 --> 00:00:57,209
<i>Run</i>

15
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,500
<i>Until we reach</i>

16
00:01:01,501 --> 00:01:06,375
<i>Until we reach you, hey</i>

17
00:01:06,626 --> 00:01:10,500
<i>Less than legendary?</i>

18
00:01:10,501 --> 00:01:13,042
<i>No problem! It's all good!</i>

19
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:16,041
<i>Until the day we can laugh</i>

20
00:01:16,042 --> 00:01:19,333
<i>Follow the shining map</i>

21
00:01:19,334 --> 00:01:22,125
<i>So, no more hesitation, fighter</i>

22
00:01:22,250 --> 00:01:25,709
<i>It's gonna be alright</i>

23
00:01:30,334 --> 00:01:34,667
[whimsical classical music]

24
00:01:37,918 --> 00:01:39,584
Don't go ahead on your own.

25
00:01:40,250 --> 00:01:42,000
You'll just
get lost again, Zorro.

26
00:01:42,125 --> 00:01:44,042
No, I won't.
The town's right there.

27
00:01:44,709 --> 00:01:46,541
[sighs] Okay, buddy.

28
00:01:46,542 --> 00:01:49,250
Hey guys, what was up
with that big lion?

29
00:01:49,459 --> 00:01:51,416
How come it
turned into a big cat?

30
00:01:51,417 --> 00:01:53,000
No, you got it backwards.

31
00:01:53,125 --> 00:01:54,584
It turned into a lion.

32
00:01:54,709 --> 00:01:56,125
It was obviously a cat first.

33
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:57,625
It was a lion!

34
00:01:57,626 --> 00:01:58,583
It was a cat!

35
00:01:58,584 --> 00:02:00,124
- It was a lion!
- A cat!

36
00:02:00,125 --> 00:02:02,625
Who cares? Do you really
want to die on this hill?

37
00:02:02,626 --> 00:02:04,583
Just wonder
why they're all so damn big.

38
00:02:04,584 --> 00:02:07,209
I hope we can find another one
of those big rabbits.

39
00:02:08,709 --> 00:02:09,750
Something's coming.

40
00:02:09,751 --> 00:02:11,000
What? What's coming?

41
00:02:11,125 --> 00:02:13,208
Nami, get behind me!

42
00:02:13,209 --> 00:02:14,250
Huh?

43
00:02:17,709 --> 00:02:20,334
[dramatic music]

44
00:02:29,459 --> 00:02:31,167
What the hell is that thing?

45
00:02:32,417 --> 00:02:33,918
[laughs]

46
00:02:37,417 --> 00:02:39,833
A Quest in the Land of Mystery!

47
00:02:39,834 --> 00:02:41,626
The Secret of the Sun God.

48
00:02:45,918 --> 00:02:48,375
[ALL yelling]

49
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,083
[laughing]

50
00:03:00,626 --> 00:03:01,751
[rumbling]

51
00:03:01,876 --> 00:03:06,083
[guitar riff playing]

52
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:08,375
- [yelling]
- So cool!

53
00:03:12,792 --> 00:03:14,708
A giant horrible bug!

54
00:03:14,709 --> 00:03:16,833
It's a grasshopper!

55
00:03:16,834 --> 00:03:18,209
How do you make it go?

56
00:03:18,417 --> 00:03:19,958
Must be new around here.

57
00:03:19,959 --> 00:03:21,042
I ain't seen you.

58
00:03:21,292 --> 00:03:22,833
Who are you, old guy?

59
00:03:22,834 --> 00:03:23,875
And where are we?

60
00:03:23,876 --> 00:03:25,416
Hey, have you seen my crew?

61
00:03:25,417 --> 00:03:27,042
I'm gonna take it
for a test ride.

62
00:03:27,501 --> 00:03:29,125
A whole lot of questions there.

63
00:03:29,876 --> 00:03:31,501
Just tell us where we are.

64
00:03:31,792 --> 00:03:32,626
Uh.

65
00:03:33,501 --> 00:03:35,374
Sorry, but I'm in a hurry,

66
00:03:35,375 --> 00:03:37,292
so I don't have
time to sit and chat.

67
00:03:37,834 --> 00:03:41,208
Short of it is, everything here
as far as the eye can see is

68
00:03:41,209 --> 00:03:42,792
the Sun God's domain.

69
00:03:43,042 --> 00:03:44,333
Sounds important.

70
00:03:44,334 --> 00:03:45,375
A god?

71
00:03:45,542 --> 00:03:46,667
That's right.

72
00:03:46,918 --> 00:03:50,250
The Sun God created this country
and everything in it.

73
00:03:50,417 --> 00:03:52,583
Nothing happening here
escapes his notice,

74
00:03:52,584 --> 00:03:54,000
no matter how small.

75
00:03:54,584 --> 00:03:57,000
Wow! So is he strong or what?

76
00:03:57,125 --> 00:03:59,250
Of course, he's strong!
He's a god, right?

77
00:03:59,542 --> 00:04:00,625
While we're at it,

78
00:04:00,626 --> 00:04:03,000
that there's Yggdrasil,
the World Tree.

79
00:04:03,125 --> 00:04:06,542
The Sun God created this land
with Yggdrasil at its heart

80
00:04:06,667 --> 00:04:09,250
and dispatched
many smaller gods to inhabit it.

81
00:04:09,626 --> 00:04:12,334
Hence, the name,
the Land of the Gods.

82
00:04:12,667 --> 00:04:15,375
The people of this country
hold our deities in reverence.

83
00:04:15,501 --> 00:04:16,667
It's our way of life.

84
00:04:16,834 --> 00:04:18,082
Makes perfect sense.

85
00:04:18,083 --> 00:04:19,709
If that's the faith
of this land,

86
00:04:19,834 --> 00:04:22,125
we should honor it
as long as we're your guests.

87
00:04:22,250 --> 00:04:25,041
You won't catch this crew
disrespecting any gods.

88
00:04:25,042 --> 00:04:26,042
Well, that's good,

89
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:28,791
because I serve the ruler
of Bigstein Castle here,

90
00:04:28,792 --> 00:04:30,250
who is one of them gods.

91
00:04:30,375 --> 00:04:32,918
Goes by the name
of Master Iscat.

92
00:04:33,250 --> 00:04:35,124
If you so desire,

93
00:04:35,125 --> 00:04:37,917
you may be granted
an audience in due time.

94
00:04:37,918 --> 00:04:40,459
Oh, there's a person
living in there?

95
00:04:40,626 --> 00:04:42,083
No, it's a cat.

96
00:04:42,417 --> 00:04:43,375
Wait, what?

97
00:04:47,542 --> 00:04:49,666
Uh, we kicked that cat--

98
00:04:49,667 --> 00:04:51,459
Oh no, no. Shh, shh.

99
00:04:51,751 --> 00:04:53,958
All right, I really need
to get going.

100
00:04:53,959 --> 00:04:56,167
Got to feed
the Great Hedgehog Needle God.

101
00:04:56,292 --> 00:04:58,375
I'm sure he's looking
for dinner right now.

102
00:04:59,083 --> 00:05:00,501
A hedgehog?

103
00:05:04,334 --> 00:05:06,041
It's been a strange day.

104
00:05:06,042 --> 00:05:07,999
The great Rabbit Ear
God perished

105
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,792
in a fire near town earlier.

106
00:05:09,959 --> 00:05:12,166
Now I'm behind schedule
with my work.

107
00:05:12,167 --> 00:05:14,375
Actually,
the rabbit died because--

108
00:05:15,459 --> 00:05:17,876
Oh my, what a tragedy!

109
00:05:18,083 --> 00:05:19,959
[whistling]

110
00:05:20,083 --> 00:05:22,833
You guys are probably
hungry now too, I reckon.

111
00:05:22,834 --> 00:05:24,834
You should go to town
and get your fodder.

112
00:05:25,083 --> 00:05:26,375
Mine left when I was a kid.

113
00:05:26,501 --> 00:05:28,083
That means food here.

114
00:05:28,584 --> 00:05:30,542
[muffled voice]

115
00:05:31,417 --> 00:05:33,125
[laughing]

116
00:05:33,375 --> 00:05:35,167
Word of caution before I go.

117
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:39,667
If you travel in that direction,
never go beyond the castle.

118
00:05:40,042 --> 00:05:41,667
Yeah? Why is that?

119
00:05:41,792 --> 00:05:44,334
That's where the Sun God's
sacred temple lies,

120
00:05:44,501 --> 00:05:47,334
guarded by vicious soldiers
who will strike you down.

121
00:05:47,918 --> 00:05:50,834
No one who dares approach it
has ever come back alive.

122
00:05:51,209 --> 00:05:52,125
Huh?

123
00:05:52,918 --> 00:05:54,959
No, no, no,
please don't say it like that!

124
00:06:00,876 --> 00:06:03,459
Hey, get back here!

125
00:06:03,959 --> 00:06:06,833
Oh, great. Dumbass!

126
00:06:06,834 --> 00:06:09,250
Bye, grasshopper guy. Thank you!

127
00:06:09,417 --> 00:06:12,709
Oh, by the way, we're sorry.

128
00:06:14,042 --> 00:06:15,000
Huh?

129
00:06:15,501 --> 00:06:18,042
Classic Luffy,
can't resist a fight.

130
00:06:18,709 --> 00:06:20,667
Vicious soldiers
sound fun though.

131
00:06:20,792 --> 00:06:21,875
No, do not do this!

132
00:06:21,876 --> 00:06:24,125
This is exactly
why Luffy's like that!

133
00:06:24,417 --> 00:06:25,958
You are an enabler!

134
00:06:25,959 --> 00:06:27,918
Wonder who them folks were.

135
00:06:28,125 --> 00:06:29,167
Whoa!

136
00:06:30,584 --> 00:06:31,584
What?

137
00:06:31,709 --> 00:06:33,918
What the hell happened
to the castle?

138
00:06:34,209 --> 00:06:37,209
[tense music]

139
00:06:37,584 --> 00:06:40,918
[laughs] Oh boy,
I smell an adventure!

140
00:06:41,042 --> 00:06:42,876
Vicious soldiers, huh?

141
00:06:43,584 --> 00:06:47,918
Gods? Let's do this already!

142
00:06:48,334 --> 00:06:49,250
I see him!

143
00:06:49,417 --> 00:06:50,625
Wait, Luffy!

144
00:06:50,626 --> 00:06:52,667
At least give Nami
some time to rest!

145
00:06:52,834 --> 00:06:54,209
It's no use, Sanji.

146
00:06:54,375 --> 00:06:56,751
There's no stopping him
once he gets like this.

147
00:06:56,876 --> 00:06:57,918
Too fast!

148
00:06:59,083 --> 00:07:01,667
I guess these things
aren't houses, huh?

149
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,209
Why does this dumb place
have to be so big?

150
00:07:05,792 --> 00:07:07,374
Hey, check out that castle.

151
00:07:07,375 --> 00:07:09,708
Looks exactly like the one
we just came from.

152
00:07:09,709 --> 00:07:10,751
Isn't that weird?

153
00:07:10,918 --> 00:07:12,042
You're right.

154
00:07:14,709 --> 00:07:15,584
Huh?

155
00:07:16,667 --> 00:07:18,626
Someone's running
straight for us.

156
00:07:18,876 --> 00:07:21,042
He's wearing
a cool Elbaph outfit, too.

157
00:07:21,751 --> 00:07:22,834
Mine's better.

158
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:24,834
Guess I'll just
avoid him for now.

159
00:07:30,667 --> 00:07:32,334
Man, what's this guy's problem?

160
00:07:32,542 --> 00:07:34,625
Hey, watch
where you're going, buddy!

161
00:07:34,626 --> 00:07:36,584
You better get out of my way!

162
00:07:40,501 --> 00:07:41,459
What?

163
00:07:41,584 --> 00:07:44,083
[ALL] Did Luffy
just break the sky?

164
00:07:49,292 --> 00:07:50,459
What the hell?

165
00:07:50,626 --> 00:07:52,042
How is this possible?

166
00:07:55,042 --> 00:07:55,958
No way!

167
00:07:55,959 --> 00:07:58,250
The sky over the temple
is cracking!

168
00:07:58,459 --> 00:08:01,083
Wait... the other side
is cracking too!

169
00:08:01,792 --> 00:08:03,209
What does this mean?

170
00:08:03,459 --> 00:08:06,125
Why are so many bad things
happening today?

171
00:08:10,792 --> 00:08:11,751
Huh?

172
00:08:11,876 --> 00:08:14,375
[gasping]

173
00:08:15,751 --> 00:08:16,667
The sky!

174
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,584
It's got a big hole in it!

175
00:08:20,375 --> 00:08:22,583
It's a curse on us!
It's got to be!

176
00:08:22,584 --> 00:08:24,124
It's divine retribution!

177
00:08:24,125 --> 00:08:27,708
Guys, that hedgehog and the cat
we took down were gods, right?

178
00:08:27,709 --> 00:08:29,542
We must have incurred
their wrath!

179
00:08:30,083 --> 00:08:31,083
No, look.

180
00:08:37,125 --> 00:08:39,209
[shaking]

181
00:08:45,584 --> 00:08:47,959
[gasping]

182
00:08:53,083 --> 00:08:54,125
What the...

183
00:08:54,834 --> 00:08:56,125
Everything's big.

184
00:09:02,584 --> 00:09:05,166
No doubt about it,
this is a giant's room!

185
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:07,166
We can't still
be on the ship, can we?

186
00:09:07,167 --> 00:09:08,666
That'd be completely insane.

187
00:09:08,667 --> 00:09:09,541
No way.

188
00:09:09,542 --> 00:09:11,209
It didn't have rooms like this.

189
00:09:11,584 --> 00:09:14,791
That aside, why is there
a metal fence here?

190
00:09:14,792 --> 00:09:17,125
There's probably a giant
on the other side.

191
00:09:18,501 --> 00:09:20,291
They must be
keeping us like pets,

192
00:09:20,292 --> 00:09:24,208
and this so-called country
is one big cage.

193
00:09:24,209 --> 00:09:25,417
No way.

194
00:09:25,709 --> 00:09:30,542
[jazzy music]

195
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:41,709
What was that noise?

196
00:09:42,167 --> 00:09:43,334
Hello?

197
00:09:45,334 --> 00:09:46,876
Is someone there?

198
00:09:48,125 --> 00:09:50,083
Can you help me?

199
00:09:52,209 --> 00:09:53,459
Huh?

200
00:09:54,292 --> 00:09:57,292
[cheerful music]

201
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:28,834
[metal clanking]

202
00:10:30,542 --> 00:10:31,626
Please don't fall.

203
00:10:31,918 --> 00:10:33,083
All right.

204
00:10:33,667 --> 00:10:36,250
Hey, where are you?

205
00:10:36,375 --> 00:10:37,834
I'm up here.

206
00:10:39,209 --> 00:10:40,751
Above you.

207
00:10:42,334 --> 00:10:43,667
[CHOPPER sobbing]

208
00:10:43,959 --> 00:10:45,042
Huh?

209
00:10:49,167 --> 00:10:50,918
Chopper!

210
00:10:51,125 --> 00:10:51,959
You guys!

211
00:10:52,209 --> 00:10:55,042
I'm so happy to see you!

212
00:10:57,834 --> 00:10:59,000
Is that a collar?

213
00:10:59,125 --> 00:11:00,082
What happened?

214
00:11:00,083 --> 00:11:01,417
I don't know!

215
00:11:01,542 --> 00:11:05,374
It was on me when I woke up
and I was in this weird place!

216
00:11:05,375 --> 00:11:07,374
The iron on the collar
is really thick,

217
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:08,751
so I couldn't get it off!

218
00:11:09,334 --> 00:11:12,334
I was so scared,
I thought I was going to die!

219
00:11:12,459 --> 00:11:13,459
Don't move.

220
00:11:14,626 --> 00:11:16,082
I'll cut it off for you.

221
00:11:16,083 --> 00:11:17,249
Please don't!

222
00:11:17,250 --> 00:11:19,459
Let's try a gentler approach.

223
00:11:21,083 --> 00:11:22,292
And there you go.

224
00:11:22,417 --> 00:11:23,416
Nice!

225
00:11:23,417 --> 00:11:25,125
Don't doubt the cat burglar.

226
00:11:30,334 --> 00:11:31,583
Thank you!

227
00:11:31,584 --> 00:11:33,667
You poor thing, you're safe now.

228
00:11:33,792 --> 00:11:35,292
There's no need to cry.

229
00:11:35,584 --> 00:11:37,709
You can pay me
for the help later.

230
00:11:38,125 --> 00:11:40,249
Hey, didn't you
just get help too?

231
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:41,542
Yes, but that was me.

232
00:11:44,334 --> 00:11:46,167
This is clearly a giant's room.

233
00:11:46,292 --> 00:11:48,416
But there are
human clothes here.

234
00:11:48,417 --> 00:11:50,541
Does that mean
they've been treating people

235
00:11:50,542 --> 00:11:51,833
like dress-up dolls?

236
00:11:51,834 --> 00:11:54,374
If that's the case,
then this giant has a real knack

237
00:11:54,375 --> 00:11:55,417
for sewing clothes.

238
00:11:55,584 --> 00:11:58,042
I admire your attention
to detail, Sun God.

239
00:11:58,209 --> 00:11:59,542
Ya big creep.

240
00:12:09,501 --> 00:12:10,584
What are you doing?

241
00:12:12,626 --> 00:12:14,292
Check it out, Sanji!

242
00:12:14,501 --> 00:12:16,375
There's a bunch of toy blocks!

243
00:12:18,209 --> 00:12:19,334
No surprise.

244
00:12:19,501 --> 00:12:21,501
The whole country's made
of those.

245
00:12:21,792 --> 00:12:24,666
That's why it smelled so bad
when you grilled that rabbit,

246
00:12:24,667 --> 00:12:26,918
because you were melting
those plastic blocks.

247
00:12:27,501 --> 00:12:30,375
Also, think about the sky
you ran into back there.

248
00:12:31,209 --> 00:12:33,709
Seemed like the road
we saw went on forever.

249
00:12:34,417 --> 00:12:36,042
But it was just a reflection.

250
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:37,501
Like a mirror?

251
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,542
So that jerk
with the cool outfit was me?

252
00:12:41,167 --> 00:12:42,083
Uh-huh.

253
00:12:42,459 --> 00:12:43,334
Take a look.

254
00:12:43,709 --> 00:12:44,584
Huh?

255
00:12:47,417 --> 00:12:48,959
You can see right through!

256
00:12:49,417 --> 00:12:52,083
It looks like a normal sheet
of glass from this side.

257
00:12:52,209 --> 00:12:55,209
I had no idea
such a magical mirror existed.

258
00:12:58,792 --> 00:13:00,459
- Say, Nami.
- Hmm?

259
00:13:00,626 --> 00:13:03,374
Next time allow me
to clean the women's kitchen--

260
00:13:03,375 --> 00:13:04,792
Do not touch our mirror!

261
00:13:05,417 --> 00:13:07,500
So some weirdo giant built

262
00:13:07,501 --> 00:13:09,583
that Block Kingdom
as a big cage,

263
00:13:09,584 --> 00:13:11,999
then they tossed
a bunch of humans and animals in

264
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,292
just to watch them for fun?

265
00:13:13,459 --> 00:13:14,792
That's really freaky,

266
00:13:15,292 --> 00:13:18,082
but that might mean
that we're in Elbaph already.

267
00:13:18,083 --> 00:13:20,750
This could be a giant's house
in the Giant's Kingdom.

268
00:13:20,751 --> 00:13:21,917
[LUFFY] Oh, really?

269
00:13:21,918 --> 00:13:23,000
Great!

270
00:13:23,792 --> 00:13:25,834
As long as we made it,
we're good.

271
00:13:26,292 --> 00:13:28,209
[LUFFY] Woohoo! Elbaph!

272
00:13:31,042 --> 00:13:32,999
I wouldn't start
celebrating yet.

273
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,125
We know this room
belongs to a giant,

274
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:37,125
but that's all we've got
at the moment.

275
00:13:37,375 --> 00:13:39,209
I guess we'll have to
check outside.

276
00:13:39,459 --> 00:13:40,792
Where's everyone else?

277
00:13:41,083 --> 00:13:43,167
We should leave
before the giant gets back.

278
00:13:43,375 --> 00:13:44,999
I say we go back inside

279
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,125
and talk to the people
in town first.

280
00:13:48,918 --> 00:13:50,750
No matter how weird this guy is,

281
00:13:50,751 --> 00:13:53,042
we're not starting trouble
with the giants.

282
00:13:53,584 --> 00:13:55,626
Hey, Luffy, you hear that?

283
00:13:56,042 --> 00:13:58,542
We've busted up enough stuff.

284
00:14:00,125 --> 00:14:02,167
Is it cool if I bust
this thing up though?

285
00:14:02,292 --> 00:14:04,666
[ALL screaming]

286
00:14:04,667 --> 00:14:06,667
Yes and hurry!

287
00:14:09,167 --> 00:14:10,541
Guys, look down!

288
00:14:10,542 --> 00:14:11,959
Giant mice!

289
00:14:12,083 --> 00:14:12,918
What?

290
00:14:13,250 --> 00:14:15,292
No, no, stop!

291
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,834
No! They can climb!

292
00:14:20,626 --> 00:14:22,250
There's a crow, too!

293
00:14:24,334 --> 00:14:25,959
[BOTH] You're here!

294
00:14:26,792 --> 00:14:28,083
What's with these things?

295
00:14:28,209 --> 00:14:29,584
Are they the soldiers?

296
00:14:29,709 --> 00:14:31,833
That would explain
why no one has come back

297
00:14:31,834 --> 00:14:33,209
from the temple alive, huh?

298
00:14:33,334 --> 00:14:36,751
What kind of a temple has
a bunch of giant monsters in it?

299
00:14:36,876 --> 00:14:39,291
You guys ate a big rabbit
earlier, right?

300
00:14:39,292 --> 00:14:41,667
I really hope
you're still hungry!

301
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:01,000
[heavy footsteps]

302
00:15:09,584 --> 00:15:11,374
Bust them all up and fast!

303
00:15:11,375 --> 00:15:13,792
The Sun God can
come back any minute!

304
00:15:14,501 --> 00:15:15,834
[LUFFY laughs]

305
00:15:16,125 --> 00:15:18,626
All right, let's do this!

306
00:15:27,834 --> 00:15:30,834
[LUFFY keeps laughing]

307
00:15:53,918 --> 00:15:56,667
I hope you're ready
to go for a ride!

308
00:16:20,292 --> 00:16:23,292
[LUFFY keeps laughing]

309
00:16:29,167 --> 00:16:31,292
Hold on, you rats.
I need a smoke.

310
00:16:38,209 --> 00:16:41,209
[dramatic music]

311
00:16:45,834 --> 00:16:47,209
I said wait!

312
00:16:47,459 --> 00:16:48,959
Learn some manners!

313
00:16:52,334 --> 00:16:55,334
[dramatic music]

314
00:17:02,209 --> 00:17:04,334
Chopper, can you
take me up there?

315
00:17:06,292 --> 00:17:07,541
No problem.

316
00:17:07,542 --> 00:17:08,959
But why? What's there?

317
00:17:09,292 --> 00:17:11,959
[laughs] The smell of treasure.

318
00:17:28,125 --> 00:17:29,000
Huh?

319
00:17:38,959 --> 00:17:42,125
Hey, whose bright idea
was it to start a fire?

320
00:17:42,250 --> 00:17:43,792
Luffy, rein it in!

321
00:17:43,918 --> 00:17:45,125
It's the fireplace!

322
00:17:45,250 --> 00:17:46,667
It's not my fault!

323
00:17:58,125 --> 00:18:00,042
[ALL] What?

324
00:18:01,918 --> 00:18:03,751
Is that the Sun God?

325
00:18:07,334 --> 00:18:11,209
My temple, my precious temple.

326
00:18:11,918 --> 00:18:13,334
Time's up, Luffy!

327
00:18:13,667 --> 00:18:15,501
Looks like the Sun God's back!

328
00:18:15,751 --> 00:18:16,709
Let's fuck it!

329
00:18:17,250 --> 00:18:18,542
Oh, okay.

330
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,584
I'll be right there!

331
00:18:25,542 --> 00:18:26,584
Go.

332
00:18:26,876 --> 00:18:28,584
Almost done over here, too.

333
00:18:37,501 --> 00:18:39,375
Muginn!

334
00:18:44,042 --> 00:18:46,250
Gum-Gum...

335
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:51,375
Dawn Pistol!

336
00:18:58,501 --> 00:19:00,459
Hilmungardr!

337
00:19:00,876 --> 00:19:02,000
We got to hurry!

338
00:19:03,209 --> 00:19:04,333
What is all this?

339
00:19:04,334 --> 00:19:05,334
Time to go, Nami!

340
00:19:05,459 --> 00:19:06,292
Okay!

341
00:19:08,667 --> 00:19:10,751
[metal clanking]

342
00:19:11,334 --> 00:19:12,167
You ready?

343
00:19:12,292 --> 00:19:13,125
Yeah!

344
00:19:13,542 --> 00:19:14,918
Come on, Luffy!

345
00:19:27,292 --> 00:19:29,542
This is unforgivable.

346
00:19:30,626 --> 00:19:32,417
That giant is huge!

347
00:19:32,792 --> 00:19:33,626
Oh, yeah?

348
00:19:33,751 --> 00:19:35,250
You think so, Luffy?

349
00:19:36,209 --> 00:19:37,083
Look.

350
00:19:39,417 --> 00:19:40,375
Hey.

351
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:45,709
[growling]

352
00:20:00,125 --> 00:20:01,375
What do you say?

353
00:20:01,542 --> 00:20:03,501
You'll pay for that
someday, Luffy.

354
00:20:03,667 --> 00:20:04,501
Okay.

355
00:20:04,626 --> 00:20:06,250
Guys, look what I found!

356
00:20:06,459 --> 00:20:08,709
Not treasure,
but it might be handy.

357
00:20:08,959 --> 00:20:09,833
Whoa!

358
00:20:09,834 --> 00:20:12,124
Is that a blueprint
for the Block Kingdom?

359
00:20:12,125 --> 00:20:13,959
How cool! Like a map?

360
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:15,584
My specialty.

361
00:20:15,918 --> 00:20:17,334
Hell, yeah! Nice find!

362
00:20:17,459 --> 00:20:18,918
That's my Nami!

363
00:20:19,417 --> 00:20:20,250
He's here!

364
00:20:21,501 --> 00:20:24,501
[dramatic music]

365
00:20:29,125 --> 00:20:30,834
How dare you...

366
00:20:31,083 --> 00:20:34,667
How dare you ruin
my perfect kingdom!

367
00:20:35,751 --> 00:20:38,041
Okay guys,
this is what we'll do!

368
00:20:38,042 --> 00:20:40,249
Run through the barracks,
go past the castle,

369
00:20:40,250 --> 00:20:41,333
and head straight.

370
00:20:41,334 --> 00:20:43,000
We'll reach another mirror!

371
00:20:43,959 --> 00:20:46,125
Smash it
and break through the wall.

372
00:20:46,292 --> 00:20:47,375
Then we're free!

373
00:20:47,542 --> 00:20:49,959
[growling]

374
00:20:50,792 --> 00:20:53,375
All right, straight ahead!

375
00:20:54,459 --> 00:20:56,626
We're breaking out!

376
00:20:59,667 --> 00:21:01,792
Why is the ground shaking
like that?

377
00:21:03,292 --> 00:21:05,125
The Sun God is angry!

378
00:21:05,292 --> 00:21:06,709
This is his wrath!

379
00:21:11,334 --> 00:21:13,459
You can't escape from me!

380
00:21:23,667 --> 00:21:26,792
<i>With my brain consumed</i>

381
00:21:29,042 --> 00:21:32,375
<i>By all the delusion and despair</i>

382
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:38,709
<i>I'm always bound
To be a little off somehow</i>

383
00:21:38,834 --> 00:21:42,292
<i>The things that come up vividly</i>

384
00:21:42,542 --> 00:21:46,250
<i>Are always the cruel memories</i>

385
00:21:47,959 --> 00:21:49,751
<i>I gather up the scraps</i>

386
00:21:49,876 --> 00:21:51,709
<i>Of the simple boredom
Of my life</i>

387
00:21:53,375 --> 00:21:56,375
<i>I might turn
Into somebody else but me</i>

388
00:21:56,501 --> 00:22:01,375
<i>I wonder which future
Would fit someone like me now</i>

389
00:22:03,083 --> 00:22:07,541
<i>From here on</i>

390
00:22:07,542 --> 00:22:10,833
<i>No matter how hard
I try to strain my eyes</i>

391
00:22:10,834 --> 00:22:12,541
<i>I'll still see nothing anyhow</i>

392
00:22:12,542 --> 00:22:15,625
<i>I'm riding the headwind</i>

393
00:22:15,626 --> 00:22:18,209
<i>I pour it into the tear
Of destiny</i>

394
00:22:18,375 --> 00:22:22,250
<i>As I split
All the false fantasies apart</i>

395
00:22:22,417 --> 00:22:23,792
<i>And everyone's</i>

396
00:22:23,918 --> 00:22:26,291
<i>Piling up
Their own life-or-death reality</i>

397
00:22:26,292 --> 00:22:29,333
<i>All the time just like that</i>

398
00:22:29,334 --> 00:22:32,959
<i>Then tomorrow comes
Way too loud</i>

399
00:22:33,083 --> 00:22:37,375
<i>Leaving no time
Even just to pray</i>

400
00:22:38,042 --> 00:22:42,209
<i>And that future we see</i>

401
00:22:43,250 --> 00:22:47,250
<i>It all belongs to me</i>

402
00:22:55,334 --> 00:22:57,416
<i>The Straw Hats play
a deadly game of tag</i>

403
00:22:57,417 --> 00:22:59,666
<i>as they dash
across the Block Kingdom.</i>

404
00:22:59,667 --> 00:23:02,124
<i>The Sun God
pursues them relentlessly,</i>

405
00:23:02,125 --> 00:23:04,250
<i>but his true identity
remains unknown.</i>

406
00:23:04,542 --> 00:23:05,666
<i>As chaos erupts,</i>

407
00:23:05,667 --> 00:23:07,541
<i>the Straw Hats
combine their strength</i>

408
00:23:07,542 --> 00:23:10,542
<i>to help Luffy open the gate
to a new adventure.</i>

409
00:23:10,751 --> 00:23:12,459
On the next One Piece!

410
00:23:12,667 --> 00:23:14,500
Destroy the miniature garden.

411
00:23:14,501 --> 00:23:16,292
Escape Block Kingdom!

412
00:23:16,542 --> 00:23:18,626
I'm going to be
King of the Pirates!

